    {
      "id": "claim_8216a2be67224657a5f03f5176bb636e",
      "statement": "dsh-subagent is the service behind child-agent delegation: an agent hands a task to a named child, collects the finished result, and for continuable children keeps sending follow-up work across turns; children come as one-shot runs that settle with a single result or continuable children whose durable session accepts later messages and can be interrupted, and the service answers discovery without loading or resuming them.",
      "evidence": [
